From: Macktherealonereally <macdev@mackthessd.org>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:52:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] SystemUI: Optionally lock network and security tiles on the
 lock screen

AOSP lets anyone pick up a locked phone and turn Wi-Fi, mobile data,
Bluetooth, airplane mode, hotspot, NFC or USB tethering on or off from
Quick Settings on the secure lock screen (only Location and VPN ask
for an unlock). One UI has "Lock network and security" for this.

Add the same as an opt-in: when Settings.Secure
qs_lock_network_and_security is 1 and the device is locked
(KeyguardManager#isDeviceLocked, so Smart Lock "unlocked" still
counts as unlocked), a click or secondary click on one of the tiles
in config_qsLockNetworkAndSecurityTiles shows the bouncer instead,
like LocationTile does, and is replayed once the user unlocked.
Cancelling the bouncer does nothing. The tile dialogs (Internet,
Bluetooth) are opened by those clicks, so they are covered too; long
press already needs an unlock (it starts the Settings activity).

Default 0 = unchanged AOSP behaviour. The toggle lives in Settings >
Lock screen.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
